  "verbalization": "Clofedanol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Rhinitis through a chain of indications that link it to Dextromethorphan and Pentoxyverine, both of which are known to treat Rhinitis. The evidence suggests that Clofedanol may be used in the management of conditions that ultimately lead to Rhinitis, such as the Common Cold, where it is associated with Dextromethorphan and Pentoxyverine. This implies a potential role for Clofedanol in the treatment of rhinitis through its involvement in the treatment of upper respiratory infections. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Clofedanol could contribute to the development or management of rhinitis, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
